  <text>
    <body>
      <p>Thomas C. Hunter is listed as the proprietor of the <ref target="civic?id=Bush%20Inn%20hotel">Bush Inn</ref> on the corner of Bouverie and Victoria streets in the directories from 1895 to 1915 (as T. C. Hunter in 1895).</p>
      <p>In 1900 the directory also lists Thomas C. Hunter, hotel broker, at 152 Victoria Street, a few doors from the hotel. He is on the 1905 electoral roll at 170 Victoria Street, the Bush Inn's number, a victualler.</p>
      <p>See also <ref target="civic?id=Bush%20Inn%20hotel">Bush Inn</ref> and <ref target="civic?id=Hotels">Hotels</ref>.</p>
      <p><hi rend="italic">This entry is a machine-assisted first draft by Common Ground, written from the directory and electoral-roll records. Only records that are clearly the same person, at the hotel's address and in a hotel trade, are linked to it. Please correct or add to it.</hi></p>
    </body>
